From e60a52e2e6954d18964dceeb86bc20b794a9bebb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: XCH27 <49464716+XCH27@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:20:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Add provider gains a Terminal access tab listing the CLIs
 with their installed state (OV-103)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Native CLI connections leave Subscriptions for their own tab. Each card
shows whether this computer can run it (built in, installed with version,
or not installed), read once per open by running the CLI's --version; it
still connects with the CLI's own sign-in and asks for no URL or key.
Catalog labels name the CLI (Codex CLI, Claude Code…), and the Alibaba
Coding Plan card keeps its brand now that Qwen Code moved out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
